  "comments": "<p>“A new obverse with the Queen showing more mature facial features and wearing a diadem was introduced on all denominations in 1965. Two obverse dies were used in 1965, one with 138 pearls around the rim, the other with 119 pearls. To complicate matters further, the 138-pearl variety is the large-pearl variety, which in turn comes in two states, one in which the back jewel is slightly attached and a second where the jewel is detached.” - Standard Charlton catalog Volume I</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6751cdc5b1bfc.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6751cdc5b1bfc.jpg\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6751cdd648ec7.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6751cdd648ec7.jpg\"></a></p><p>“In 1977, a die change resulted in new punches and therefore new dies creating a variety in the seven for that year. The seven vary in Canada spread and are also different in size.” - Standard Charlton Catalogue Volume I</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6751ce80446d8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6751ce80446d8.jpg\"></a></p>",
